<title>FRANCE: Moroccan importers buy Canadian, Greek durum wheat.</title>
<headline>Moroccan importers buy Canadian, Greek durum wheat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Moroccan importers on Thursday bought a total of 35,000 tonnes of durum wheat for August-September delivery, European grain traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>They bought 30,000 tonnes of Canadian durum at $230 per tonne, cost and freight, and a further 5,000 tonnes of Greek durum at $225 per tonne, cost and freight, they said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
